Descriptive statistics for the demographic characteristics of the sample are shown below in Tables \ref{tab:englishStudy3} through \ref{tab:genderStudy3}. The sample contains a high majority of participants self-reporting English fluency, and 63.6\% reported having an attained an associate's degree level of education or higher. About 77\% of the sample reported being in a household with income of \$100,000 or less. With respect to gender identity, 2.8\% identified as non-binary, and the remainder of the sample was roughly split between those who endorsed ``female'' (49.6\%) and ``male'' (47.3\%); 1 participant preferred not to respond.


